  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under refill protocol RBC-RX-05. All 7 original messages and the 1 that arrived during the work are closed. Patients received replies, including corrected messages where a decision changed.\n\n- **Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg:** I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill. His August potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed (damaged) sample, so it didn't count, and I ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then a valid outside BMP from 10/20 arrived showing potassium 5.8. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0001) and placed no new lisinopril order. Your urgent task is task-t0022, and the patient got a corrected message. **He now has no active lisinopril order.** The repeat BMP order is still open. His hernia repair is set for 11/12.\n- **Samuel Price (pt-0030):**\n  - **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). He and the pharmacy sent three requests for it; one order covers them all. His eGFR is 58 after the lab's correction. An outside HbA1c from 8/19 counts as recent.\n  - **Lisinopril 20 mg:** I first renewed it, then the lab corrected his 10/06 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35% above his level before the dose increase on 9/18, which the protocol treats like a high potassium. I cancelled the renewal (mr-t0003). Your urgent task is task-t0023, and he got a corrected message. **He now has no active lisinopril order and says his supply is finished.**\n- **Marcus Webb (pt-0031):**\n  - **Lisinopril 10 mg:** 30-day supply, 0 refills (mr-t0005), and a BMP ordered (sr-t0006). His last BMP was 10/20/2025, more than 12 months ago; he had a visit 9/28/2026. A standalone potassium of 4.6 came in during the work; on its own it isn't a BMP, so the decision stands.\n  - **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The eGFR of 39 from 10/14 was entered in error (wrong patient's sample), so I used his valid eGFR of 92 from 9/28. HbA1c was 6.9% on 9/28.\n- **Leonard Kaplan (pt-0070), lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled.** His BMP on 10/19 showed creatinine 1.46, 46% above his 1.00 before the dose increase on 9/28. Your urgent task is task-t0008, about his current order mr-70002, which I left active. He was told you'll review it.\n\nWhen renewing I wrote a new order that replaced the old one, which stops the old order. That's why the cancelled renewals for Odum and Price leave them with no active lisinopril. Your tasks for them point to their earlier orders (mr-00283 and mr-00295). I wrote correction notes in both their charts and closed the three new result items for these patients that arrived during the work.\n\nYour results queue still has 9 older items I didn't touch, since they're outside the refill protocol. Two are critical potassiums that need prompt review: pt-0016 at 6.3 (task-00011) and pt-0008 at 6.4 (task-00005).",
